This is a textbook case of **coverage-without-verification** — every method is called, giving you line coverage, but almost nothing is actually asserted. Here's the severity-ranked audit:

---

## 🔴 Critical — Assert-Free Tests (fire-and-forget)

These tests call production code and **never verify the outcome**. They will pass even if the method silently does the wrong thing.

### 1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)
Calls `AddProduct` but never checks the product was stored.
```csharp
// FIX: verify the product is retrievable
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var saved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", saved!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, saved.Price);
```

### 2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)
Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price actually changed. A no-op `Save()` would still pass.
```csharp
// FIX: verify new price persisted
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
```

### 3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)
Calls `RemoveProduct` but never verifies deletion. The product could still exist.
```csharp
// FIX: verify product is gone
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

### 4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)
Calls `GetProductCount` on an **empty catalog** and discards the result. Two bugs hidden: no data setup, no assertion.
```csharp
// FIX: seed data, assert count
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

### 5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)
Applies a 10% discount but never checks the resulting prices. A discount of 0%, 100%, or even a price increase would pass.
```csharp
// FIX: verify discounted prices
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

### 6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)
Imports CSV but never checks the products were created. Parsing could silently fail or store garbage.
```csharp
// FIX: verify imported product
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var p = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", p!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, p.Price);
```

---

